                <pb facs="0445" n="375" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg375"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/2415: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-12-26T19:00:00-05:00">December 26, 1934—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>111. Rio Pact has passed Colombian House of Representatives. Most of the
                    Conservatives were absent during the voting. Some hope is felt that it may pass
                    the Senate by similar methods.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
